To know when to descend is actually quite an important skill. The usual
answer is that whenever you see stairs, go down for a quick look, because
(apart from a more technical reason) then you know the position of the
upstairs should you fall through a hole. In general, try to explore the
accesible rooms and then continue downwards. It pays to explore an upper
level more thoroughly, including searching for secret doors and corridors,
if you know that there has to be a shop somewhere, or if you cannot
continue further down because you get beaten up. However, if you linger
too much on the upper levels, you will only get a higher experience level
(meaning that the monsters get tougher), but not necessarily better
equipment (meaning that it gets harder to kill those monsters.)

